  "body": "**4.21.2 staged the install correctly but never completed it.** PATCH `4.21.2` → `4.21.3`.\n\n## What was wrong with my own fix\n\nUnder `$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'`, a native command writing to **stderr** raises a terminating `NativeCommandError` in PowerShell — and `uv` writes its progress there.\n\nThe helper died on uv's first `Resolved 79 packages in 367ms` line: before installing anything, and before writing its result file. So the update silently never happened, and the dashboard had nothing to report either.\n\n```\nuv.EXE : Resolved 79 packages in 367ms\n    + CategoryInfo          : NotSpecified: (...) [], RemoteException\n    + FullyQualifiedErrorId : NativeCommandError\n```\n\nThe native call now runs with `Continue` in effect and is judged by **exit code alone**, restoring `Stop` afterwards for the cmdlets that follow.\n\n## Verified against a real install\n\nReproduced in an isolated `UV_TOOL_DIR`, so nothing on the host was touched.\n\n**Original bug confirmed** — running `uv tool install --force` from inside the target environment:\n```\nerror: failed to remove directory `...\\tools\\free-claude-code\\Scripts`: Access is denied. (os error 5)\n```\nand the aftermath — uv had already deleted `site-packages` before failing:\n```\nPackageNotFoundError: No package metadata was found for free-claude-code\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'free_claude_code'\n```\nThat is exactly the reported corruption.\n\n**With this change**, same scenario: stages, exits cleanly with the old version still working, and the helper then installs for real:\n```json\n{ \"ok\": true, \"exit_code\": 0, \"message\": \"Deferred install completed.\" }\n```\n`4.21.1 → 4.21.2`, environment intact and `fcc-server --version` working.\n\n## Important limitation\n\n**This cannot help an install still running 4.21.1 or earlier.** The upgrade is performed by the code already loaded, so a user below 4.21.3 who presses the button still runs the old in-place path and still gets the corruption. They must update once from the install script; after that the button is safe.\n\nThat's inherent to self-updating and worth stating plainly in the release notes rather than leaving people to discover it.\n\n## Verification\n\nNew regression test asserts the native call runs under `Continue` and that success is taken from `$LASTEXITCODE` — the precise trap that broke it. Full suite passes except the 14 failures that also fail on unmodified `main`.\n\n## Residual risks\n\nThe captured `output` still contains the `NativeCommandError` text as a non-terminating error record, because `2>&1` merges stderr into the stream. Cosmetic — the install completes and the exit code is authoritative — but it makes the stored log noisier than it needs to be.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
