    "message": "fix(updates): stop the deferred Windows helper dying on uv's stderr\n\n4.21.2 staged the install correctly but never completed it. Under\n$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop', a native command writing to stderr raises a\nterminating NativeCommandError in PowerShell -- and uv writes its progress\nthere. The helper therefore died on uv's first \"Resolved N packages\" line,\nbefore installing anything and before writing its result file, so the update\nsilently never happened and the dashboard had nothing to report.\n\nThe native call now runs with 'Continue' in effect and is judged by exit code\nalone, restoring 'Stop' afterwards for the cmdlets that follow.\n\nVerified against a real install in an isolated UV_TOOL_DIR, which reproduces the\noriginal bug exactly: running uv tool install --force from inside the target\nenvironment fails with \"failed to remove directory ...\\Scripts: Access is\ndenied. (os error 5)\" and leaves site-packages already deleted -- ModuleNotFound\non the next start. With this change the same scenario stages, exits cleanly with\nthe old version still working, and the helper then installs 4.21.1 -> 4.21.2\nwith ok=true and exit_code=0.\n\nNote this fix cannot help an installation that is still running 4.21.1 or\nearlier: the upgrade is performed by the code already loaded, so anyone below\n4.21.3 must update once from the install script before the button is safe.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
